# Write a Rocdown page

Rocdown keeps prose portable and makes executable regions visible. Start with
ordinary Markdown, then add a document-root declaration only where the page
needs structure or behavior.

## Start with page metadata

````rocdown
@page {
    route: "/guides/hello/",
    draft: False,
    meta: {
        title: "Hello from Rocdown",
        description: "A small Markdown-first page",
    },
}

# Hello from Rocdown

This paragraph is ordinary Markdown.
````

Rocdown can derive routes from file paths, so documentation sites usually omit
`route`. Use an explicit route when an existing URL must stay stable.

## Display code safely

Fenced code is always display-only, even if the language is `roc`, `rocci`, or
`rocdown`:

````markdown
```roc
answer = 42
```
````

This rule prevents a documentation example from silently becoming build-time
or runtime code.

## Add Roc values and components

For standalone Rocdown preview, a page can colocate Roc and Rocci:

````rocdown
@roc {
published = "2026-08-16"
}

@component Byline = |{ date }|
    <p>Published {date}</p>

# Article title

<Byline date={published} />
````

`@roc` holds Roc values and helpers. On `live` pages, import `pf.Sqlite` in
`@roc` and call those helpers from `@patch` / `@command` / `@init`. Document-root component
tags and directives are explicit islands in the Markdown stream. Inline HTML in
a Markdown paragraph is disabled by default.

`rocdown build` accepts `static` pages (Markdown, `@page`, and article blocks),
splices pure Rocci on `hydrate` pages, and emits Datastar plus an island
service for `live` pages. `@use` stays a site-build error. See
[Publish a hybrid Rocdown site](/rocdown/hybrid/).

For asides, steps, includes, and tabs, see
[Write documentation components](/rocdown/article-blocks/).

## Link pages

Standalone previews understand wiki links, Rocdown file links, and nested
relative Markdown links:

```markdown
See [[Interactive]] or [the interactive guide](Interactive.rocdown).

This plan follows [the product-boundary decision](knowledge/decisions/consolidate-rocdown-product-boundary.md).
```

For a Rocdown site, stable absolute routes are the clearest current form:

```markdown
Read the [Rocdown reference](/rocdown/language/).
```

## Preview and publish

Preview one page and the documents it links to:

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- run docs/guide.rocdown
```

Standalone preview uses the default Paper (or selected) reading shell. Pages
with H2 or H3 headings get a left “On this page” navigator that scrolls to the
same heading IDs. Rocdown site builds keep a separate right-hand outline inside
documentation chrome.

Build a static documentation tree:

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- build docs
```

Rocdown reads `docs/rocdown.toml`, validates its curated navigation, compiles the
Rocdown site theme, and writes the configured output directory atomically.
